The chain at one window ($\exists\mathrm{Al}_T\iff\lamW>0\iff[\lamA>0\wedge\mathfrak G_T\succ0]\Rightarrow\mathrm{KEP}(T)$ indeterminate $\Rightarrow\lamW\ge0$) & \textsc{proved}; indeterminacy is not claimed equivalent to either end; $\mathrm{RD}_T\Rightarrow\lamP\ge0$ per window, the effective window shift for $\zeta$ and the converse for $\zeta$ at $T>0.8$ \textsc{open}\\
Remark~\ref{rem:Cheb} (on $\PT$ the prime comb is the Chebyshev remainder) & the identity \eqref{eq:Cheb} \textsc{proved}; the closing sentences a reading\\
The entry law for $\Aconst$ and the two scales of \S\ref{subsec:where}, and the class monotonicity $\mathcal W_{T'}\subseteq\Wcl$ & \textsc{proved} (elementary)\\
The \textsc{diagnostic} record of Appendix~\ref{app:diag} & \textsc{diagnostic} throughout; no proof depends on it\\
\end{longtable}}

\subsection{Reproduction}
The certificate of Theorem~\ref{thm:C} is archived, in the repository of the programme, under
\path{03-research/phase-154-row-d-law-of-the-body/scripts/} as
\path{round5/certificate/CERT_log3_R5.json}
(all $u_j$, $a_j$ as exact decimal strings, $\beta_0,\beta_1$, $M_2$, target, minimal width,
segment statistics, interval enclosures), with the round-4 predecessor
\path{round4/certificate/CERT_log3_M24.json}. The verifier is \texttt{round5/r5bb.py}
(second-order cover, no cap, no discard) with \texttt{r5core.py} (symbol, exact derivatives of
$\gh0,\gh1$) and \texttt{round4/r4iv.py} (interval enclosures of $m$, $\psi'(\frac14)$, $H_0,H_1$,
$k_0,k_1$); \texttt{r5final.py} performs the float-versus-interval comparison and writes the
archive. The data of Theorem~\ref{thm:N} --- the pairs $(\tau_0,q)$, the interval endpoints of $a,b_0,b_1$, the
quadrature orders and the remainder bounds for each $M$ --- and the witnesses, moment polygon and
constants $r_0,V^\star$ of Theorem~\ref{thm:Bbeta}, together with the numbers of
Corollary~\ref{cor:SC1} and of the measured ceilings, are archived with the accompanying scripts; each
of those computations runs in well under a minute on one core. The enclosures of Theorem~\ref{thm:N}
are \path{03-research/phase-155-row-d-flat-kernel-criterion/scripts/r2_a_enclosure_M<M>.json},
$M\in\{3,5,6,7,8\}$, written by \texttt{r2\_a\_enclosure.py}; the $\beta$-box of
Theorem~\ref{thm:Bbeta} at $\frac12\log3$ is \path{r2_c_beta_bound.json} there, and at the two-prime
windows \path{scripts/r3b/r3b_beta_box.json} (written by \texttt{betabox.py}). The enclosures of
Theorem~\ref{thm:Np} are the sixteen files per window \path{scripts/r3b/r3b_enclosure_<T>_M<M>.json},
$T\in\{0.68,\log2\}$, $M\in\{6,7,9,11,13,14,\dots,24\}$, written by \texttt{r3b\_enclosure.py}
(field \texttt{ceiling\_upper\_bound}). The certificate of Theorem~\ref{thm:w11} is
\path{scripts/r3c/r3c_04_enclosure_iv.json}, written by \texttt{r3c\_04\_enclosure\_iv.py} from the
